 {'id':'L22-COVERAGE-03','status':'open','sourcePages':[675,678,691],'finding':'Retaining armature inductance adds an electrical current state, and retaining flexible motion adds mechanical modes. These source points occur in assumptions/explanations, but no answer requires selecting the correct retained state/order. One concrete comparison of angle+speed versus angle+speed+current and an explicitly added flexible coordinate would test this meaningful modeling consequence. Keep the model assumptions and state list explicit; do not claim every real joint has exactly a fixed order.'},
 {'id':'L22-COVERAGE-04','status':'bounded-accounting-note','sourcePages':list(range(669,695)),'finding':'All 26 actual pages inspected. Pages669–671 are title/objective/contents and693–694 reference/closing. Pages672–690 are substantive;691–692 recap prior content. The waveform, all seven effective-parameter table rows, actual code state, solver argument order, missing setup, vectorized array operation and source numerical discrepancy were checked. Repetitions or mere extraction do not establish additional coverage. The illustrated arm-length annotations on p672 are descriptive dimensions, not parameters used in this lecture’s one-joint model; no padding quiz is requested for them.'}
